   Egg interactions are now part of the "sitting" patch.
http://www.contrib.andrew.cmu.edu/~ajo/free-software/nethack/sit343.diff

   I decided that the "It feels comfortable" message was kind of weird.
The new interactions are:

   (1) If you're in the proper "mother" form (e.g., a female red dragon
if the egg is a red dragon egg), you incubate it, which speeds up its
timer by rnd(20) turns each time you #sit.
   (2) If it's not your egg, you "feel somehow out of place".
   (3) If the egg is sterilized, you "feel sad for a moment".
   (4) If you're a heavy monster of the wrong species (e.g., a wumpus
or a blue dragon, but not a male red dragon), you splat the egg.
   (5) Otherwise, it's "not very comfortable", and nothing else happens.
(This is the old behavior for all the above cases.)

   The patch still includes heavy monsters breaking open chests;
pit-sitting; and sitting in a pie to get a YAFM. The only
non-egg-related change is that I've made it so that if you break
a chest open by sitting on it, and it's trapped, you'll get hit by
the trap (and you'll never get "The poisoned needle misses!", because
there's no way it'd miss such a huge target).

   I've submitted the updated patch to the NH Patch Database.
Comments welcome. (No "dragon sitting on gold" YAOIs please; that's
already in a different patch, and I'm not too keen on it myself.)

